CUBRID Gateway uses the bundled unixODBC driver manager library.
The libraries are licensed under LGPL 2.1. See ../libodbc_license.txt and the
copyright notices and license files in @THIRDPARTY_UNIXODBC_ARCHIVE@.
The archive contains the complete unmodified upstream source, including libltdl.
CUBRID does not install the unixODBC command-line programs from this archive.

The producer used these compilers:
  C: @CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID@ @CMAKE_C_COMPILER_VERSION@
  C++: @CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID@ @CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_VERSION@

To rebuild the library, extract the archive and configure in a separate directory
with matching compilers. Replace the placeholder paths below with local paths:

  CC=<C-compiler> CXX=<C++-compiler> <source>/configure --prefix=<staging-prefix>
  make AUTOCONF=: AUTOHEADER=: AUTOMAKE=: ACLOCAL=:
  make install AUTOCONF=: AUTOHEADER=: AUTOMAKE=: ACLOCAL=:

The resulting lib/libodbc.so.2 and its versioned payload can replace the installed
copy when they provide a compatible interface. Gateway loads the copy in its
installation's lib directory.

Provide the database-specific ODBC driver separately and register it in
odbcinst.ini. Set ODBCSYSINI to that file's directory before starting Gateway.
